1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:03,558
September 1st, 1939.

2
00:00:03,728 --> 00:00:06,221
4:45 in the morning.

3
00:00:06,591 --> 00:00:11,301
A German battleship, on a so-called
friendly visit to the port of Danzig,

4
00:00:11,351 --> 00:00:14,666
turns its guns toward a
small Polish army post.

5
00:00:15,386 --> 00:00:16,483
And fires.

6
00:00:17,953 --> 00:00:19,395
Over the next six years,

7
00:00:19,445 --> 00:00:23,237
this war will spread to almost
every corner of the world.

8
00:00:23,607 --> 00:00:28,658
It will kill somewhere between sixty
and eighty-five million people.

9
00:00:29,028 --> 00:00:31,882
And it will end with a new kind of weapon,

10
00:00:31,932 --> 00:00:35,707
so powerful that one bomb
can destroy a whole city.

11
00:00:36,977 --> 00:00:38,791
So how did the world get here,

12
00:00:38,841 --> 00:00:43,191
just twenty years after the war
that was supposed to end all wars?

13
00:00:46,861 --> 00:00:49,354
Rewind to 1919.

14
00:00:49,724 --> 00:00:53,147
World War One is over,
and Germany has lost.

15
00:00:53,517 --> 00:00:58,717
At the Treaty of Versailles, the winners
make Germany accept responsibility

16
00:00:58,767 --> 00:01:03,917
for the war, give up land, shrink
its army and pay huge sums of money.

17
00:01:04,787 --> 00:01:07,280
Many Germans feel humiliated.

18
00:01:07,650 --> 00:01:11,128
Then, in 1929, the American
stock market crashes,

19
00:01:11,178 --> 00:01:15,027
and the Great Depression
spreads around the world.

20
00:01:15,397 --> 00:01:18,123
In Germany, millions lose their jobs.

21
00:01:18,493 --> 00:01:23,125
Angry, hungry people start listening
to a man who promises to restore

22
00:01:23,175 --> 00:01:26,247
Germany's pride, and who
blames Jews and other

23
00:01:26,297 --> 00:01:29,125
minorities for the country's problems.

24
00:01:29,495 --> 00:01:31,756
His name is Adolf Hitler.

25
00:01:32,926 --> 00:01:36,742
In January 1933, he becomes
Germany's chancellor,

26
00:01:36,792 --> 00:01:41,698
and within months he turns the
country into a dictatorship.

27
00:01:42,068 --> 00:01:45,259
He's not the only one with big ambitions.

28
00:01:45,629 --> 00:01:52,070
In Italy, the dictator Benito
Mussolini dreams of a new Roman Empire,

29
00:01:52,120 --> 00:01:55,098
and invades Ethiopia in 1935.

30
00:01:55,468 --> 00:01:59,980
In Asia, Japan's army
seizes Manchuria in 1931,

31
00:02:00,030 --> 00:02:04,938
then launches a full-scale
war on China in 1937.

32
00:02:05,308 --> 00:02:06,638
Hitler starts small.

33
00:02:07,008 --> 00:02:10,897
He rebuilds the army,
far beyond what the treaty allowed.

34
00:02:11,267 --> 00:02:14,553
In 1936, he sends troops
into the Rhineland,

35
00:02:14,603 --> 00:02:18,643
a zone that was supposed
to stay free of soldiers.

36
00:02:19,013 --> 00:02:21,274
Britain and France do nothing.

37
00:02:21,644 --> 00:02:25,300
In 1938, he takes over Austria.

38
00:02:25,670 --> 00:02:28,628
Then he demands part of Czechoslovakia.

39
00:02:28,998 --> 00:02:32,118
At a meeting in Munich,
Britain and France agree,

40
00:02:32,168 --> 00:02:34,747
hoping this will be his last demand.

41
00:02:35,117 --> 00:02:38,385
The British Prime Minister,
Neville Chamberlain,

42
00:02:38,435 --> 00:02:41,796
flies home and promises
"peace for our time".

43
00:02:42,166 --> 00:02:47,450
Less than six months later, Hitler seizes
what's left of Czechoslovakia anyway.

44
00:02:48,520 --> 00:02:52,873
Then, in August 1939,
comes the biggest shock.

45
00:02:53,243 --> 00:02:56,048
Hitler makes a deal with his sworn enemy,

46
00:02:56,098 --> 00:02:59,690
Joseph Stalin, the dictator
of the Soviet Union.

47
00:03:00,060 --> 00:03:03,018
They promise not to attack each other.

48
00:03:03,388 --> 00:03:08,439
And in secret, they agree to split
Poland and Eastern Europe between them.

49
00:03:09,609 --> 00:03:13,265
Nine days later,
the guns at Danzig open fire.

50
00:03:16,535 --> 00:03:21,121
Germany smashes into Poland with tanks,
planes and fast-moving troops.

51
00:03:21,491 --> 00:03:23,519
Newspapers call it Blitzkrieg.

52
00:03:23,689 --> 00:03:24,786
Lightning war.

53
00:03:25,856 --> 00:03:30,210
Two days later, Britain and
France declare war on Germany.

54
00:03:30,580 --> 00:03:35,631
On September 17th, the Soviet
Union invades Poland from the east.

55
00:03:36,001 --> 00:03:39,889
Within five weeks, Poland
is defeated and divided.

56
00:03:40,259 --> 00:03:42,985
Then, in the west, almost nothing happens.

57
00:03:43,355 --> 00:03:45,848
For months, the armies just sit and wait.

58
00:03:46,018 --> 00:03:48,278
People call it the Phoney War.

59
00:03:48,648 --> 00:03:54,165
In April 1940, Hitler strikes again,
invading Denmark and Norway.

60
00:03:54,535 --> 00:03:57,615
Then, on May 10th, Germany
attacks the Netherlands,

61
00:03:57,665 --> 00:03:59,818
Belgium, Luxembourg and France.

62
00:04:00,188 --> 00:04:04,289
France has built a giant wall of
forts along the German border,

63
00:04:04,339 --> 00:04:06,170
called the Maginot Line.

64
00:04:06,540 --> 00:04:11,035
But the main German tank force goes around
it, through the thick Ardennes forest,

65
00:04:11,085 --> 00:04:13,917
where the French believed
tanks couldn't pass.

66
00:04:14,287 --> 00:04:17,710
In just ten days, German tanks
reach the English Channel.

67
00:04:18,080 --> 00:04:21,207
Hundreds of thousands of
British and French soldiers

68
00:04:21,257 --> 00:04:23,829
are trapped on the beaches at Dunkirk.

69
00:04:24,199 --> 00:04:26,692
Britain sends everything that floats.

70
00:04:26,862 --> 00:04:30,517
Warships, ferries, fishing boats,
even small pleasure yachts.

71
00:04:30,887 --> 00:04:35,466
In about nine days, more than three
hundred and thirty thousand soldiers

72
00:04:35,516 --> 00:04:37,567
are carried back to Britain.

73
00:04:37,937 --> 00:04:39,964
But France is finished.

74
00:04:41,134 --> 00:04:45,023
On June 22nd, France signs an armistice.

75
00:04:45,393 --> 00:04:50,272
Hitler makes them sign it in
the very same railway carriage

76
00:04:50,322 --> 00:04:54,165
where Germany signed
the armistice in 1918.

77
00:04:54,535 --> 00:04:58,191
Now Britain and its
Commonwealth stand almost alone.

78
00:04:58,561 --> 00:05:03,379
Its new Prime Minister, Winston
Churchill, refuses to make peace.

79
00:05:03,749 --> 00:05:07,851
So the German air force tries to
destroy Britain's Royal Air Force,

80
00:05:07,901 --> 00:05:10,196
to clear the way for an invasion.

81
00:05:10,566 --> 00:05:12,826
This is the Battle of Britain.

82
00:05:13,796 --> 00:05:18,847
But Britain has a chain of radar stations
that can see German planes coming.

83
00:05:19,217 --> 00:05:21,515
By autumn, the invasion is called off,

84
00:05:21,565 --> 00:05:24,966
and German bombers pound
Britain's cities at night.

85
00:05:29,036 --> 00:05:32,460
Then Hitler makes the
biggest gamble of the war.

86
00:05:32,830 --> 00:05:40,206
On June 22nd, 1941, he breaks his deal
with Stalin and invades the Soviet Union.

87
00:05:40,576 --> 00:05:42,943
More than three million soldiers attack,

88
00:05:42,993 --> 00:05:46,325
along a front from the
Baltic Sea to the Black Sea.

89
00:05:46,695 --> 00:05:49,653
It's called Operation Barbarossa.

90
00:05:50,023 --> 00:05:51,353
At first, it works.

91
00:05:51,723 --> 00:05:55,214
Millions of Soviet soldiers
are killed or captured,

92
00:05:55,264 --> 00:05:59,333
and by December, German troops
are just outside Moscow.

93
00:05:59,703 --> 00:06:04,289
Exhausted, short of supplies, and
slowed by autumn mud, the Germans stall.

94
00:06:04,459 --> 00:06:06,254
Then winter arrives.

95
00:06:07,224 --> 00:06:09,769
Temperatures fall below minus thirty,

96
00:06:09,819 --> 00:06:14,136
and many German soldiers still
don't have winter uniforms.

97
00:06:14,506 --> 00:06:17,157
On December 5th,
the Soviets counter-attack,

98
00:06:17,207 --> 00:06:19,790
and push the Germans back from Moscow.

99
00:06:20,160 --> 00:06:23,393
Two days later, on the
other side of the world,

100
00:06:23,443 --> 00:06:28,234
Japan attacks the American naval
base at Pearl Harbor, in Hawaii.

101
00:06:28,604 --> 00:06:34,353
Japan hopes to knock out the American
fleet before America can fight back.

102
00:06:34,723 --> 00:06:39,076
More than two thousand four
hundred Americans are killed.

103
00:06:39,446 --> 00:06:43,567
The next day, the United
States declares war on Japan.

104
00:06:43,937 --> 00:06:49,453
And on December 11th, Hitler declares
war on the United States too.

105
00:06:49,823 --> 00:06:52,084
Now it really is a world war.

106
00:06:53,354 --> 00:06:57,707
On one side, the Axis:
Germany, Italy and Japan.

107
00:06:58,077 --> 00:07:01,701
On the other, the Allies:
Britain, the Soviet Union,

108
00:07:01,751 --> 00:07:04,757
the United States, China and many more.

109
00:07:08,027 --> 00:07:12,380
In early 1942, the Axis looks unstoppable.

110
00:07:12,750 --> 00:07:16,406
Japan sweeps across Southeast
Asia and the Pacific.

111
00:07:16,776 --> 00:07:22,060
But American codebreakers have
learned where Japan will strike next.

112
00:07:22,230 --> 00:07:24,723
A tiny island called Midway.

113
00:07:25,093 --> 00:07:31,330
On June 4th, 1942, American dive bombers
find the Japanese aircraft carriers,

114
00:07:31,380 --> 00:07:35,958
and in about five minutes,
three of them are on fire.

115
00:07:36,328 --> 00:07:39,983
By the next morning, Japan has
lost four aircraft carriers.

116
00:07:40,153 --> 00:07:43,112
And its navy never fully recovers.

117
00:07:44,182 --> 00:07:49,725
In North Africa, British and Commonwealth
troops beat Germany's most famous general,

118
00:07:49,775 --> 00:07:52,489
Erwin Rommel, at El Alamein in Egypt.

119
00:07:52,859 --> 00:07:56,595
But the biggest battle of
all is in the Soviet Union,

120
00:07:56,645 --> 00:07:59,538
at a city named after Stalin himself.

121
00:07:59,708 --> 00:08:00,805
Stalingrad.

122
00:08:01,175 --> 00:08:05,580
From August 1942, the two
sides fight for every street,

123
00:08:05,630 --> 00:08:08,552
every building, even every floor.

124
00:08:08,922 --> 00:08:13,508
In November, the Soviets surround
the entire German Sixth Army.

125
00:08:13,878 --> 00:08:16,139
Hitler forbids it to retreat.

126
00:08:16,509 --> 00:08:21,560
On February 2nd, 1943,
the last German troops surrender.

127
00:08:22,530 --> 00:08:26,069
Of the hundreds of thousands
who were surrounded,

128
00:08:26,119 --> 00:08:30,837
only about ninety-one thousand
are left to be taken prisoner.

129
00:08:31,207 --> 00:08:35,095
From now on, in the east,
Germany is mostly retreating.

130
00:08:35,465 --> 00:08:40,981
That summer, at Kursk, the Soviets win one
of the biggest tank battles in history.

131
00:08:41,351 --> 00:08:44,217
At sea, German submarines
called U-boats try

132
00:08:44,267 --> 00:08:47,565
to starve Britain by
sinking its supply ships.

133
00:08:47,935 --> 00:08:52,201
But British codebreakers at Bletchley
Park, including Alan Turing,

134
00:08:52,251 --> 00:08:55,078
building on the work
of Polish codebreakers,

135
00:08:55,128 --> 00:08:57,405
crack the German Enigma cipher.

136
00:08:57,775 --> 00:09:02,361
By the middle of 1943,
the U-boats are losing.

137
00:09:05,631 --> 00:09:08,098
While armies fight on the battlefields,

138
00:09:08,148 --> 00:09:12,078
something far darker is
happening behind the front lines.

139
00:09:12,820 --> 00:09:18,103
Nazi Germany and its collaborators
are carrying out the Holocaust.

140
00:09:18,525 --> 00:09:22,646
A plan to murder every
Jewish person in Europe.

141
00:09:23,388 --> 00:09:26,943
Jews are forced into crowded
ghettos, shot in mass killings,

142
00:09:26,993 --> 00:09:30,067
or sent by train to death
camps like Auschwitz.

143
00:09:30,809 --> 00:09:34,930
Six million Jewish men,
women and children are murdered.

144
00:09:37,672 --> 00:09:42,290
Millions of others are killed too,
including Roma and Sinti people,

145
00:09:42,340 --> 00:09:46,910
disabled people, Polish civilians
and Soviet prisoners of war.

146
00:09:47,652 --> 00:09:51,540
It is one of the worst
crimes in human history.

147
00:09:57,382 --> 00:10:01,735
In July 1943, the Allies land in Sicily.

148
00:10:02,105 --> 00:10:06,924
Mussolini is overthrown,
and in September, Italy surrenders.

149
00:10:07,294 --> 00:10:12,113
But German troops keep fighting in
Italy almost until the very end.

150
00:10:12,483 --> 00:10:16,604
Then comes the biggest invasion
from the sea in history.

151
00:10:16,974 --> 00:10:19,467
June 6th, 1944.

152
00:10:19,637 --> 00:10:20,637
D-Day.

153
00:10:21,539 --> 00:10:25,540
Around one hundred and fifty-six
thousand American, British,

154
00:10:25,590 --> 00:10:31,241
Canadian and other Allied troops land in
Normandy, in France, by sea and by air.

155
00:10:31,611 --> 00:10:34,570
On Omaha Beach, the fighting is brutal.

156
00:10:34,740 --> 00:10:37,930
But by nightfall, the Allies are ashore.

157
00:10:38,300 --> 00:10:42,574
Just over two weeks later,
the Soviets launch their own giant attack,

158
00:10:42,624 --> 00:10:47,072
Operation Bagration, and destroy
most of a whole German army group.

159
00:10:47,442 --> 00:10:50,168
In August, Paris is liberated.

160
00:10:50,538 --> 00:10:53,415
In December, Hitler
launches his last big attack

161
00:10:53,465 --> 00:10:56,519
in the west, back through
the Ardennes forest.

162
00:10:56,689 --> 00:10:58,717
The Battle of the Bulge.

163
00:10:59,087 --> 00:11:00,087
It fails.

164
00:11:00,922 --> 00:11:04,896
In the Pacific, the Americans
hop from island to island,

165
00:11:04,946 --> 00:11:07,136
closer and closer to Japan.

166
00:11:07,506 --> 00:11:14,185
In China, millions of soldiers have held
down most of Japan's army since 1937.

167
00:11:14,355 --> 00:11:18,244
And in Burma, British and
Indian troops drive Japan back.

168
00:11:18,614 --> 00:11:22,264
At Iwo Jima and Okinawa,
the fighting is so fierce

169
00:11:22,314 --> 00:11:25,817
that American leaders
fear invading Japan itself

170
00:11:25,867 --> 00:11:28,781
will cost enormous numbers of lives.

171
00:11:32,051 --> 00:11:38,265
By late April 1945, Soviet troops are
fighting in the streets of Berlin.

172
00:11:38,635 --> 00:11:42,291
On April 30th, Hitler kills
himself in his bunker.

173
00:11:44,061 --> 00:11:46,787
A week later, Germany surrenders.

174
00:11:47,157 --> 00:11:50,580
May 8th becomes Victory in Europe Day.

175
00:11:50,750 --> 00:11:52,545
In Moscow, it's May 9th.

176
00:11:52,915 --> 00:11:54,478
But Japan fights on.

177
00:11:54,848 --> 00:12:00,321
On August 6th, 1945, an American
bomber drops an atomic bomb

178
00:12:00,371 --> 00:12:02,922
on the city of Hiroshima.

179
00:12:03,292 --> 00:12:07,413
Two days later, the Soviet
Union declares war on Japan.

180
00:12:07,783 --> 00:12:12,137
And the next day, a second
atomic bomb destroys Nagasaki.

181
00:12:13,507 --> 00:12:16,648
By the end of the year,
the two bombs have killed

182
00:12:16,698 --> 00:12:19,488
as many as two hundred thousand people.

183
00:12:21,458 --> 00:12:24,988
On August 15th, Emperor
Hirohito tells his people

184
00:12:25,038 --> 00:12:28,137
on the radio that Japan will surrender.

185
00:12:28,507 --> 00:12:33,934
And on September 2nd, 1945,
aboard the battleship USS Missouri,

186
00:12:33,984 --> 00:12:36,582
the war is officially over.

187
00:12:41,252 --> 00:12:44,907
World War Two is the deadliest
war in human history.

188
00:12:45,277 --> 00:12:50,329
The Soviet Union alone loses
around twenty-seven million people.

189
00:12:50,699 --> 00:12:53,657
China loses more than fifteen million.

190
00:12:54,027 --> 00:12:59,311
In total, somewhere between sixty
and eighty-five million people die.

191
00:12:59,481 --> 00:13:01,276
Most of them civilians.

192
00:13:02,646 --> 00:13:06,327
Out of the ruins, the winners
create the United Nations,

193
00:13:06,377 --> 00:13:09,092
to stop it from ever happening again.

194
00:13:09,462 --> 00:13:13,698
Nazi leaders are put on trial
at Nuremberg for their crimes,

195
00:13:13,748 --> 00:13:16,141
and Japanese leaders in Tokyo.

196
00:13:16,511 --> 00:13:19,466
And the United States
and the Soviet Union,

197
00:13:19,516 --> 00:13:23,888
allies just months before,
become rivals in a new Cold War.

198
00:13:24,258 --> 00:13:27,914
So here's the question
historians still argue about.

199
00:13:28,284 --> 00:13:31,242
When did Germany really lose the war?

200
00:13:32,212 --> 00:13:35,868
Was it the day Hitler
invaded the Soviet Union?

201
00:13:36,038 --> 00:13:38,298
The day America joined?

202
00:13:38,468 --> 00:13:41,194
Or in the frozen streets of Stalingrad?

203
00:13:41,564 --> 00:13:44,987
Tell me your answer,
and your reason, in the comments.

